# Lakebase (Postgres Autoscaling) — BYO project/branch for BricksBot.
#
# The App binds Lakebase via variables in databricks.yml:
#   lakebase_branch   → projects/<project>/branches/<branch>
#   lakebase_database → …/databases/<database>
#
# Those values are NOT committed. Put them in gitignored `dev.local.yml`
# (copy from `dev.local.yml.example`) or pass `--var` / `BUNDLE_VAR_*`.
#
# Create or reuse a project (workspace project limits apply):
#
#   databricks postgres list-projects -p <profile>
#   databricks postgres create-project bricksbot \
#     --json '{"spec":{"display_name":"BricksBot"}}' -p <profile>
#   databricks postgres list-branches projects/<project-id> -p <profile>
#   databricks postgres list-databases projects/<project-id>/branches/<branch-id> -p <profile>
#
# Default database id is usually `databricks-postgres`.
# Schema `bricksbot` is created by the App service principal on first deploy
# (deploy the App before pointing local `npm run dev` at Lakebase).
#
# Without Lakebase env (`LAKEBASE_ENDPOINT` / `PGHOST`), the server uses an
# in-memory store — fine for UI work and most unit tests.
